In article <2996@unocss.unomaha.edu> tdavis@unocss.unomaha.edu (tdavis) writes:
>
>     The 730 refuses to boot; in fact, all it displays on the console
>is a CONV011 code.  Now, from a book that I've scrounged up, it says
>the 730 will print 'CONSOLE', and then place you at the >>> prompt. 
>If the system does not print out 'CONSOLE', it means one of the self
>tests failed.  The book had no other help concerning what the error
>could be.
>

According to the _VAX-11/730 Hardware User's Guide_, the 730 performs
self-tests at power up.  It prints one of the letters from "CONSO"
between each test, and the letters "LE" after all the test are passed.
According to the _VAX-11/730 Installation Guide_, the book to check is
the _VAX-11/730 Diagnostic System Overview Manual_.  That should tell
you what the error code means.  Unfortunately, I cannot seem to find
my copy of that.  I last saw it in with all my VAX/VMS v3.2 stuff, but
I can't lay my hands on it now.  Maybe somebody out there has an
accesible copy of it?  Good luck.

