In article <1938@mtecv2.mty.itesm.mx> josevela@mtecv2.mty.itesm.mx (Jose Angel Vela Avila) writes:
> 
>   Does anyone knows how can I get the version and the "drivers" running on my
>   VAX 6310 ?

I'm not sure exactly what you are after, but the "version" is typed out when
when you boot the system, is contained in the file /sys/conf/newvers.sh and
can be viewed online by something like: echo "version?S" | adb /vmunix.

You can't explicitly tell what "version" of Ultrix the drivers are from. Except
in the case of a botched or installation or incremental upgrade, they are
replaced along with the OS.  The command "what /vmunix" will reveal the sccs
version id's of all the module in the kernel, including drivers, but you have
no way of correlating these id's with the system "version".

